      "writtenOn": "2026-09-08T17:04:52Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "We call `onBrokerApiStarted()` when the broker is already available (via `start()`).\nThe same `onBrokerApiStarted()` method can be invoked via `BrokerApiPluginListener`.\n\nIs it possible (theoretically) that both paths fire for the same broker so that the consumer could subscribe to the same topic more than once?\n\nShould we not make `onBrokerApiStarted()` idempotent to avoid that?",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 82,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 82,
        "endChar": 27
      },
      "revId": "ead363356322245c4bd8c99c6e10287ddbdb3f65",
      "serverId": "d5d70762-12d0-45a1-890d-524b12d3f735"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "9bde9915_24f75bb9",
        "filename": "src/main/java/com/gerritforge/gerrit/plugins/replication/pull/event/EventsBrokerMessageConsumer.java",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 82,
      "author": {
        "id": 1020677
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-09-08T17:16:38Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "If the concrete implementation of the broker is already loaded then `onBrokerApiStarted` will only be called in this `start` method (as `isBrokerApiStarted` will be true).\n\nIf, as it should be, the concrete implementation hasn\u0027t loaded yet, then `onBrokerApiStarted` will only be called in the listener `BrokerApiPluginListener`. \n\nI don\u0027t see how this could be called twice for the exact same instance of the same plugin?",
      "parentUuid": "a26c3879_5ca0fbc4",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 82,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 82,
        "endChar": 27
      },
      "revId": "ead363356322245c4bd8c99c6e10287ddbdb3f65",
      "serverId": "d5d70762-12d0-45a1-890d-524b12d3f735"
    },
    {
